# Café Queene — Website

A multi-page website for **Café Queene**, a coffee shop and kitchen with branches in **Middelburg** and **Nelspruit**, owned by Queene Mavuso. Built for the WEDE5020 Web Development (Introduction) POE.

- **GitHub repository:** https://github.com/Thandazo-Mavuso/CafeQueene
- **Live website:** _add the Netlify / GitHub Pages link here after deployment (Part 3)_

## Pages

| Page | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `index.html` | Home: hero, highlights, story teaser, branches |
| `about.html` | The Café Queene story, owner, photo gallery with lightbox and values |
| `menu.html` | Full menu with prices, loaded by JavaScript with search, category filter and sort |
| `enquiry.html` | FAQ accordion and a validated enquiry form, sent with AJAX, with an instant cost and availability response |
| `contact.html` | Branch addresses, phone numbers, emails, opening hours, maps and a validated contact form that builds an email |

## Project structure

```
CafeQueene/
├── index.html
├── about.html
├── menu.html
├── enquiry.html
├── contact.html
├── README.md
├── robots.txt         (tells search engines what they may crawl)
├── sitemap.xml        (lists every page for search engines)
├── _headers           (security and caching headers, used by Netlify)
├── css/
│   └── style.css      (one shared stylesheet, CSS variables for the palette)
├── js/
│   └── main.js        (all JavaScript: mobile navigation, dynamic menu, forms)
└── images/            (photos, favicon.svg and og-image.jpg for social sharing)
    └── thumbs/        (small 600px copies used by the gallery for faster loading)
```

## Design

- **Palette (from the proposal):** terracotta `#c1502e` and `#a13f22`, cream `#fdf8f0` and `#f5ede1`, dark grey `#2e2e2e`.
- **Fonts:** Zilla Slab for headings and Nunito Sans for body text (Google Fonts).
- **Responsive breakpoints:** desktop (1025px and up), tablet (up to 1024px), phone (up to 600px) and a small-phone rule for about 320px. The navigation turns into a hamburger menu at 768px and below.
- **Accessibility:** skip-to-content link, visible keyboard focus styles, labelled form fields, descriptive alt text, titles on map frames, and `aria-expanded` / `aria-controls` on the menu button.

## Changelog

Newest entries first.

### Part 3 — SEO, page speed and security (1 November 2026)

**On-page SEO**
- Wrote a unique title tag (under 60 characters) and meta description (110 to 160 characters) for every page, using the keywords in the table below.
- Fixed the heading structure: one `<h1>` per page and no skipped levels. The home page jumped from `<h1>` to `<h3>`, so a hidden "Menu highlights" heading was added and the "More than just a café" and "What We Stand For" labels became real `<h2>` headings. The footer headings changed from `<h4>` to `<h2>`.
- Added a keyword line above the home page heading ("Coffee shop & kitchen in Middelburg & Nelspruit").
- Image optimisation: descriptive file names (for example `menu-signature-breakfast.jpg`), alt text on every image, and `width` and `height` on every image so the page does not jump while loading.
- Added links between pages inside the text (About to Menu and Enquiry, Menu to Enquiry and Contact, Contact to Enquiry, Enquiry to Menu).
- Page addresses stay short and descriptive (`/menu.html`, `/contact.html`), with a `canonical` link on every page.
- Added Open Graph and Twitter card tags and a 1200 by 630 share image, so links look good on WhatsApp, Facebook and X.
- Added structured data (JSON-LD): an Organization and WebSite entry on the home page, and a `CafeOrCoffeeShop` entry for each branch on the contact page, with address, phone, opening hours and map position, so search engines can show them in local results.
- Changed the page language to `en-ZA`, added a favicon and a theme colour.

**Additional requests**
- Created `robots.txt` and `sitemap.xml` (all five pages).
- Page speed (see the table below): resized and compressed 22 photos to the size they are shown at, made small thumbnails for the gallery, lazy-loaded images below the screen, gave the home photo `fetchpriority="high"`, loaded all scripts with `defer`, removed two heavy Google Maps iframes, and added caching rules in `_headers`.
- Security (see the list below): a Content Security Policy on every page, referrer policy, integrity hashes on the Leaflet files, a spam trap on both forms, and removal of every inline style and script.

### Part 3 — Interactive elements and animations (1 November 2026)

All of this JavaScript is in `js/main.js` (sections 5 to 8) and the styling is in `css/style.css`.

- **Interactive map (`contact.html`):** replaced the two Google Maps iframes with one Leaflet map (version 1.9.4, loaded from a CDN with integrity hashes) using OpenStreetMap tiles. Both branches have markers with popups showing the name, address and hours, and three buttons (Both branches, Middelburg, Nelspruit) fly the map to the chosen place. The popups are built with DOM methods, not HTML strings. If the library fails to load, a message appears and each branch card still has an "Open in Google Maps" link. The marker positions are approximate town-centre coordinates.
- **FAQ accordion (`enquiry.html`):** five questions, each a `<button>` with `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls`. Only one answer is open at a time, and the arrow, Home and End keys move between questions.
- **Photo gallery with lightbox (`about.html`):** eight photos in a responsive grid. Clicking one opens a larger version in a `<dialog>` element with previous and next buttons, arrow-key navigation, a caption with the photo number, and the Escape key or the close button to leave. Focus returns to the thumbnail that was clicked. Thumbnails in `images/thumbs/` are small copies (about 356 KB for all eight) so the page loads faster.
- **Animations:** cards and sections fade in as they scroll into view (`IntersectionObserver` with a short stagger), cards lift slightly on hover, the accordion panels slide in, and gallery photos zoom a little on hover. All animation is switched off for people who set "reduce motion" on their device.
- **Back-to-top button:** created with JavaScript (`createElement`), shown after scrolling down 600px, and scrolls smoothly to the top.
- **Advanced DOM manipulation:** creating elements, adding classes, setting attributes, listening to scroll and keyboard events and moving focus, used across the map, accordion, lightbox, menu and form code.
- Removed the Google Maps iframes, which also reduces page weight.

### Part 3 — JavaScript merged into one file (1 November 2026)

- Combined `js/menu.js` and `js/forms.js` into `js/main.js`, so the site has one stylesheet and one script, and every page now loads only `js/main.js`.
- `main.js` is split into numbered sections (start-up, mobile navigation, dynamic menu, forms). One `DOMContentLoaded` block calls `initMobileNav()`, `initMenu()` and `initForms()`. Each of these first checks that its page's elements exist, so the menu and form code does nothing on pages that don't use it.
- Removed the extra `<script>` tags from `menu.html`, `enquiry.html` and `contact.html` and deleted `menu.js` and `forms.js`.
- All features were tested again after the merge (navigation on all five pages, menu search, filter and sort, enquiry and contact forms) with no JavaScript errors.

### Part 3 — Forms, validation and AJAX (1 November 2026)

- Created the forms script (now merged into `js/main.js`), shared by both forms. Each field names its rule in a `data-rule` attribute (name, email, phone, select, date, guests, message) and the script checks it.
- **Client-side validation:** names (2 to 60 letters), email format, South African phone numbers (`082 123 4567` or `+27 82 123 4567`), dates that are not in the past and within 12 months, guests from 1 to 50, and messages of 10 to 500 characters. HTML5 attributes (`required`, `type="email"`, `type="date"`, `min`, `max`, `maxlength`) are also on the fields.
- **Error handling:** every field has its own error message under it (`role="alert"`), the field gets `aria-invalid="true"`, and the first invalid field receives focus. Fields are checked when the user leaves them and re-checked while typing. A live character counter shows the message length.
- **enquiry.html:** added phone, enquiry type, preferred date and number of guests. After a valid submit the page shows an instant response with the estimated cost, availability for the chosen date (using the branch opening hours) and what happens next. Date and guests become optional for general questions.
- **AJAX submission:** the enquiry is sent with `fetch()` as a POST request, so the page does not reload. While sending, the button is disabled and shows "Sending…". If the request fails, an error message with both phone numbers is shown and the form stays filled in.
- **contact.html:** this page had no form, so a new one was added (name, email, optional phone, type of message, branch, message). After validation the page builds the email (To, Subject and Message), shows a preview, and offers an "Open in my email app" button using a `mailto:` link addressed to the chosen branch. The form's `action` is a `mailto:` address as a fallback.
- **Security:** both forms contain a hidden spam-trap field. The scripts write user text with `textContent`, never `innerHTML`, so typed text cannot inject HTML.
- Problem found: the old enquiry form used `action="#"`, so submitting only reloaded the page. It now has a real action.
- **Note:** until a real Formspree form ID replaces `YOUR_FORM_ID` in the form's action, the enquiry runs in demo mode (validated, response shown, nothing sent).

### Part 3 — Dynamic menu with search, filter and sort (30 October 2026)

- Created the menu script (now merged into `js/main.js`). The 22 menu items (name, description, price, category) now live in a JavaScript array and are built onto the page with DOM methods (`createElement`, `appendChild`, `textContent`) instead of being typed into the HTML.
- Added a search box that filters items by name or description as the user types (not case sensitive).
- Added category filter buttons (All, Coffee & Drinks, Breakfast, Lunch, Fast Food, Snacks & Sweets) that use `aria-pressed` to show the active filter.
- Added a sort menu: menu order, price low to high, price high to low, and name A to Z.
- Added a result count that screen readers announce (`aria-live="polite"`), an empty-state message with a "Clear search and filters" button, and a `<noscript>` message.
- The large section photos are hidden while the user is searching so the results stay compact.
- Rebuilt `menu.html` with CSS classes (`.menu-section`, `.menu-item`, `.filter-btn` and others) instead of inline styles, which also removed about 150 lines of repeated inline CSS.

### Part 3 — Feedback corrections (30 October 2026)

Part 2 was marked 84/100. The lecturer's feedback listed six priority improvements. Each one is addressed below.

**Feedback 1 — Complete the mobile navigation**
- Added a hamburger `<button class="nav__toggle">` to all five pages, with `aria-controls="primary-nav"`, `aria-expanded` and an `aria-label` that changes between "Open" and "Close".
- Wrote the `.nav__toggle` and `.nav__links.is-open` CSS. At 768px and below the links collapse into a vertical list that opens under the logo, and the three bars animate into an X.
- Created `js/main.js` to toggle the `is-open` class, keep `aria-expanded` in sync, close the menu with the Escape key, and reset the menu if the window is widened.
- Problem found: the old nav had a `.nav__toggle { display: none; }` rule but no button and no script, so phones just showed the full desktop links.

**Feedback 2 — Strengthen responsive design**
- Replaced the single 968px breakpoint with separate tablet (1024px), tablet-portrait (768px), phone (600px) and small-phone (360px) breakpoints.
- Adjusted navigation, section spacing, logo and heading sizes, buttons (full width on phones), cards, form padding and map height (250px down to 220px).
- Problem found: the contact page used inline `grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr)`, which overrode the stylesheet, so the two branch cards never stacked on phones. Moving it into the stylesheet fixed this.
- Problem found: the About page had a 3-item values list inside a 4-column grid. Added a `.features__grid--three` modifier.

**Feedback 5 — Improve interaction accessibility**
- Added `:focus-visible` outlines for links, buttons, inputs, selects and textareas, plus a lighter outline on the dark footer.
- Added a "Skip to main content" link at the top of every page, and `id="main"` on each `<main>`.
- Removed the inline styles from `contact.html` and `enquiry.html` and moved them into named classes (`.form-card`, `.form-group`, `.form-control`, `.branch-card--detailed`, `.map-embed`, `.page-intro` and others).
- Branch headings on the contact page changed from `h3` to `h2` so the heading order is h1 → h2.
- Added `title` attributes to both map iframes and `autocomplete` attributes to the enquiry form fields.

**Other corrections found while editing**
- `.text-center` was used on several pages but never defined in the stylesheet, so some eyebrow labels were left-aligned. Added the rule.
- The About page showed literal `**Middelburg**` asterisks. Replaced them with `<strong>` tags.

**Feedback 3 — Complete the changelog:** this section and the entries below.
**Feedback 4 — Improve Git history:** changes were committed in several small commits with descriptive messages (see the repository history).
**Feedback 6 — Document testing:** see the Testing section below.

